course: dictionary
lesson: 8029
title: Bent light: refraction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Light usually travels in straight lines. When light passes from one material into another, such as from air into water or glass, it changes direction. This bending of light is called refraction.
explain: «A straw in water looks bent because light changes direction as it passes from water to air.» The straw is not really bent. The light coming from it bends at the surface, so your eyes see the straw in a slightly wrong place. The look is an illusion.
explain: Refraction is the name for the bending itself. You will hear it in science lessons as «refraction of light» or «light refracts». Sound and water waves can refract too, but light is the main case you will study first.
fact: Refraction is the bending of light when it passes from one material into another.
fact: Light changes direction when it moves from air into water or glass.
fact: Refraction explains why a straw in a glass of water looks bent or broken.
fact: Refraction helps make rainbows and lets lenses in glasses and magnifying glasses work.
fact: Pools can look shallower than they really are because of refraction.
exercise: «A straw in water looks bent because light changes direction as it passes from water to air.» What is this bending of light called? | *Refraction | Shadow | Echo | Reflection
exercise: What happens to light when it passes from air into water? | It stops completely | It gets louder | *It changes direction and bends | It turns into sound
exercise: Why does a straw in a glass of water look bent? | The straw is made of glass | The straw is really bent | *Light bends as it passes from water into air | The water is too cold
test: Which of these is something refraction helps to explain in science? | Thunder | Snow | Footprints | *Rainbows
test: «Light refracts» is a phrase from science. What does refracts mean here? | Stops moving | Turns into a shadow | *Bends as it passes into another material | Makes a loud noise
exam: A pupil says, «A pool looks shallower than it really is.» Which best explains this? | Light stops at the surface | The water is too cold | The pool is painted blue | *Refraction, because light bends as it leaves the water
